Now I understand the D task. The issue: after successful PATCH the page just reloads — the user reported "страница ничего не показывает и не обновляется" (page shows nothing and doesn't update). Actually reload should update... but the user says the page shows nothing. Hmm, possibly because `window.location.reload()` inside `.then()` — that should work. But the user says "data saved but page shows nothing and doesn't update". Maybe the reload happens but... Actually maybe the issue is the PATCH returns 200 with body, and reload works — but the user observed no visible feedback. Regardless, the task D requirement is clear:

- After successful PATCH show «Сохранено» AND update the card or reload.
- On error show the API error text.
- Same for channel and ACL.
- Test: static check that handlers use a status element; if node available, JS test via `node --test` with fetch/DOM mock. Node v24 is available!

Design for D:
1. Add a status element per row in my_videos.html (e.g. `<span class="row-status" data-status-for="{{ row.id }}"></span>` in actions cell or near). And in the edit form, a status element. Simpler: add one status element per row: `<span class="save-status" hidden></span>`.
2. manage.js: on PATCH success → set status text «Сохранено» and reload after a short delay (or update card in place). Simplest robust: show «Сохранено» in the row status element, then reload after ~600ms so the user sees feedback. On error → show err.message in the status element (class form-error) instead of only toast.
3. Same for acl-form POST, acl-remove, is_private change.
4. channel.js: add a success status element (`#channel-edit-status`) next to error box; on success show «Сохранено» then reload; on error show err.message (already done).

For the test: node --test with fetch/DOM mock. Writing a full DOM mock in node is heavy. Alternative: static check in pytest (handlers reference a status element) + a node --test that loads manage.js with a minimal fake DOM. Node has no DOM. I'd need to stub document/window. manage.js is an IIFE that queries `.my-videos` table and attaches listeners. I can build a tiny fake DOM: document.querySelector returns a fake table object with addEventListener capturing handlers, etc. That's doable but fiddly. 

Given "минимум: статическая проверка, что обработчики используют элемент статуса; если в окружении есть node, JS-тест через node --test с подменой fetch и DOM" — node IS available, so I should write a node --test. Let me design a small harness:

- Create tests/js/helpers.mjs? Or a single test file tests/js/manage.test.mjs that:
  - builds a minimal DOM stub: elements with classList, addEventListener, getAttribute, closest, nextElementSibling, hidden, textContent.
  - sets global.window = { tzApi: {...mock}, tzToast: fn, location: {...}, confirm }, global.document = stub.
  - loads manage.js source via fs.readFileSync + eval in a context... manage.js references `document`, `window`, `Element`, `HTMLFormElement`, `FormData`. Node 24 has FormData global. Element/HTMLFormElement don't exist — the code does `t instanceof Element`. I can define global.Element = class {}, global.HTMLFormElement = class {} and make my fake elements instances.

That's feasible. The test: simulate submit of edit-form → mock tzApi.patch resolves → assert status element got «Сохранено» and location.reload called (or card updated). And error path: patch rejects with {message} → status shows message.

But manage.js currently does `window.location.reload()` immediately on success — no status. My change: show status, then reload after delay (setTimeout) — in node test, setTimeout exists; I can await a tick.

Simpler contract for the JS: on success, set `statusEl.textContent = "Сохранено"`, then `setTimeout(function(){ window.location.reload(); }, 600)`. In node test, I can use fake timers? No — just wait 700ms in test, or make delay a var. Or: update the card in place AND show status, skip reload. Task says "обновляй карточку или перезагружай страницу" — reload is fine, but must show «Сохранено» first. I'll do: show status, then reload after 700ms.

For node test determinism, I'll have manage.js use `window.tzReload()` helper? Keep simple: `setTimeout(..., 700)`. In the test, await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 800)) then assert reload called. That's fine (sub-second test).

Let me design the manage.js changes:

In my_videos.html, add to the actions cell (`mv-actions`) a status span:
`<span class="save-status" data-save-status hidden></span>` — per row. And the edit-row form gets its own? The row's status span suffices for all row actions (edit, acl, privacy) since rowOf() gives the row.

manage.js: helper `function statusOf(row) { return row.querySelector("[data-save-status]"); }` — wait, row is the tr; the span is in the actions td inside the row, so `row.querySelector(".save-status")` works. For edit-form submit, form is in the NEXT row (edit-row), so rowOf(form) → form.closest("tr[data-video-id]") → the edit-row has no data-video-id! rowOf returns null for edit-form. Current code: `rowOf(form)` — form's closest tr is the edit-row which lacks data-video-id → row null → return! Wait, that means the edit-form submit handler never works?? Let me check: `rowOf = btn => btn.closest("tr[data-video-id]")`. The edit form is in `<tr class="edit-row" hidden>` — no data-video-id. So `rowOf(form)` → null → `if (!row) return;` — the PATCH never fires! That's bug #2 root cause! The edit button toggles editRow, but submit finds no row → returns silently. That explains "PATCH returns 200" — no wait, if it returns early, PATCH wouldn't fire at all. But user said PATCH returned 200 and data saved... Hmm, user said "запросы PATCH /api/videos/{id} ... возвращают 200, данные сохраняются, но страница ничего не показывает". So PATCH did fire. Let me re-check rowOf: `btn.closest("tr[data-video-id]")` — closest looks at the element itself and ancestors. The form is inside `<td>` inside `<tr class="edit-row">`. That tr has no data-video-id, but its PREVIOUS sibling tr does — closest doesn't go to siblings. So row = null. Unless... the edit-row tr is nested? No. Hmm, but then PATCH wouldn't fire. But the user observed PATCH 200. Maybe the user tested via the privacy checkbox and channel form. Or maybe `closest` from the form... no.

Wait, maybe I misread — let me recheck the template: `<tr data-video-id>` then `<tr class="edit-row" hidden>` with the form. The submit listener is on `table`, event target = form. `rowOf(form)` = form.closest("tr[data-video-id]") = null (edit-row has no attr, tbody/table don't either). So `if (!row) return;` → handler returns. So edit-form PATCH never fires from this page?! But the user saw PATCH 200... Maybe from is_private checkbox (change event, rowOf(t) works since checkbox is in the data row) — yes! The privacy checkbox PATCH fires and reloads. And the user may have clicked "Сохранить" — but that silently does nothing... Actually wait — maybe I misread and edit-row is INSIDE the data row? Let me re-read: lines 12-44 is `<tr data-video-id>...</tr>`, then line 45 `<tr class="edit-row" hidden>` — sibling. So yes, rowOf(form) is null.

Hmm, but the user explicitly said PATCH /api/videos/{id} returned 200 and data saved. That could be from the is_private toggle. Or the user tested edit and it did fire... Let me look again at the submit handler:

```
table.addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
    var form = e.target;
    if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement)) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    var row = rowOf(form);
    if (!row) return;
```

So for edit-form, row = null → return AFTER preventDefault. So no PATCH. The user might have observed PATCH from the checkbox. Either way, there's a real bug: edit-form can't find its row. Fix: give the edit-row a data-video-id too, or find the previous sibling. Simplest: add `data-video-id="{{ row.id }}"` to the edit-row tr as well. Then rowOf(form) works.

OK so D fix for manage.js:
1. my_videos.html: add `data-video-id="{{ row.id }}"` to edit-row tr, and add `<span class="save-status" hidden></span>` in the actions td (and maybe in the edit form row too — the status in the main row is enough since we can query from the row).
2. manage.js:
   - `function statusOf(row) { return row ? row.querySelector(".save-status") : null; }`
   - `function showStatus(row, msg, isErr) { var el = statusOf(row); if (!el) return; el.textContent = msg; el.hidden = false; el.classList.toggle("form-error", !!isErr); }`
   - edit-form submit: on success → showStatus(row, "Сохранено") then setTimeout reload 700ms; on error → showStatus(row, err.message, true) (plus toast optional).
   - acl-form post: same.
   - is_private change: same.
   - del/acl-remove: keep reload on success (delete removes the row anyway); error → status too. Task says "То же для канала и ACL" — ACL add/remove should show status. del can reload.
3. channel.js: add success status element `#channel-edit-status` in channel.html next to error box; on success show «Сохранено» + delayed reload; error already shows err.message in errBox.

Test (pytest static + node --test):
- Static: manage.js contains ".save-status" / showStatus usage; my_videos.html has data-save-status or class save-status; channel.html has channel-edit-status; channel.js references channel-edit-status and "Сохранено".
- Node test: tests/js/manage.test.mjs + channel.test.mjs with fake DOM. Let me write one node test file covering manage.js edit-form success/error and channel.js success/error.

Node harness: I'll write tests/js/dom-stub.mjs exporting a function to build a fake DOM from a simple spec, and set globals. Then test files import manage.js source via `new Function` or `vm.runInThisContext` after setting globals.

Let me write the harness carefully:

```js
// tests/js/harness.mjs
import fs from "node:fs";
import vm from "node:vm";

export class FakeClassList {
  constructor() { this._set = new Set(); }
  add(...c) { c.forEach(x => this._set.add(x)); }
  remove(...c) { c.forEach(x => this._set.delete(x)); }
  toggle(c, force) { const has = force === undefined ? !this._set.has(c) : force; has ? this._set.add(c) : this._set.delete(c); return has; }
  contains(c) { return this._set.has(c); }
}

let idSeq = 0;
export class FakeElement {
  constructor(tag = "div", attrs = {}) {
    this.tagName = tag.toUpperCase();
    this.attributes = { ...attrs };
    this.classList = new FakeClassList();
    (attrs.class || "").split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).forEach(c => this.classList.add(c));
    this.children = [];
    this.parent = null;
    this.hidden = !!attrs.hidden;
    this.textContent = "";
    this.dataset = {};
    this._listeners = {};
    this.id = attrs.id || "";
    this.name = attrs.name || "";
    this.checked = false;
  }
  getAttribute(k) { return k in this.attributes ? this.attributes[k] : null; }
  setAttribute(k, v) { this.attributes[k] = String(v); }
  addEventListener(type, fn) { (this._listeners[type] ||= []).push(fn); }
  dispatch(type, event) { (this._listeners[type] || []).forEach(fn => fn(event)); }
  appendChild(c) { c.parent = this; this.children.push(c); return c; }
  closest(sel) {
    // supports "tr[data-video-id]" and ".class"
    let el = this;
    while (el) {
      if (matches(el, sel)) return el;
      el = el.parent;
    }
    return null;
  }
  querySelector(sel) { return query(this, sel)[0] || null; }
  querySelectorAll(sel) { return query(this, sel); }
  get nextElementSibling() {
    if (!this.parent) return null;
    const sibs = this.parent.children;
    const i = sibs.indexOf(this);
    return sibs[i + 1] || null;
  }
}
```

matches(el, sel): handle `tr[data-video-id]` → tag tr and attr present; `.cls` → classList contains; `[data-save-status]` → attr; `.thumb img` descendant — needed for app.js but I'm not testing app.js here. For manage.js: selectors used: ".my-videos", "tr[data-video-id]" (closest), ".edit-btn"/".del-btn"/".acl-remove" (classList.contains on target), ".edit-row", ".edit-form"/".acl-form", "[data-save-status]" via row.querySelector(".save-status"), HTMLFormElement instanceof, FormData(form) — FormData constructor with a form element: Node's FormData doesn't accept a fake element. manage.js does `new FormData(form)` — in node, `new FormData(formEl)` throws (expects HTMLFormElement). I need to stub global.FormData to read from fake form: give FakeForm a `_data` map and stub FormData:

```js
class FakeFormData {
  constructor(form) { this._f = form; }
  get(k) { return this._f._fields?.[k] ?? null; }
}
```

And `form instanceof HTMLFormElement` — set `global.HTMLFormElement = FakeForm` class; make edit/acl forms instances of it. `t instanceof Element` — set `global.Element = FakeElement`.

window: `global.window = { tzApi: {...}, tzToast(){}, location: { reload(){...}, href:"" }, confirm: () => true }`. manage.js references `window.tzApi`, `window.confirm`, `window.location`. Also bare `document`. Set `global.document = fakeDocument` where querySelector(".my-videos") returns the table.

Load script: `vm.runInThisContext(fs.readFileSync(path, "utf8"), { filename })` — the IIFE runs immediately, registering listeners on the table.

Then simulate: find edit form element, call `table.dispatch("submit", { target: form, preventDefault() {} })`. Since handler checks `form instanceof HTMLFormElement`, form must be FakeForm instance (subclass of FakeElement with HTMLFormElement). I'll create `class FakeForm extends FakeElement` and set `global.HTMLFormElement = FakeForm`; `global.Element = FakeElement` (FakeForm instanceof FakeElement ✓).

tzApi mock: `window.tzApi = Object.assign(function(){}, { patch: (path, body) => Promise.resolve({}), del: ..., post: ... })`. Record calls; for error test, patch rejects with `Object.assign(new Error("название занято"), { status: 409 })`.

Assertions:
- success: after dispatch + await flush, status element textContent === "Сохранено", and after ~800ms window.location.reload called. To avoid waiting, I can make the delay configurable? Simpler: in manage.js use `setTimeout(reload, 700)`; test waits 800ms — acceptable.
  Actually, better: instead of reload after timeout, update the card in place (title link text) AND show status, no reload? Task: "показывай «Сохранено» и обновляй карточку или перезагружай страницу". Reload after showing status satisfies both (user sees «Сохранено», then page reloads showing saved data). I'll keep delayed reload.
- error: status textContent === err.message, classList contains form-error, no reload.

For channel.js test: similar harness; channel.js queries ".channel-head" (getAttribute data-channel-id), getElementById("subscribe-btn"), "channel-edit-btn", "channel-edit-form", "channel-edit-error", "channel-edit-cancel". My fake document needs getElementById. Build: head div with attrs; form FakeForm with id channel-edit-form; errBox id channel-edit-error; status span id channel-edit-status; buttons. Dispatch submit on form. Assert status textContent "Сохранено" and errBox hidden; error path: errBox.textContent = message, status stays hidden.

document stub needs: querySelector, getElementById, querySelectorAll (app.js uses it but we're not loading app.js in these tests... manage.js uses document.querySelector only. channel.js uses querySelector + getElementById).

OK. Also the pytest static test: tests/test_frontend_d_save.py:
- my_videos.html contains 'class="save-status"' (or data attr) and edit-row has data-video-id.
